      "problem": "Simplify $\\dfrac{20}{8(z-1)}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we decompose all of the terms into their prime factors. The $20$ in the numerator  becomes $2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 5,$ and the $8(z-1)$ in the denominator becomes $2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot (z-1).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14156876/assets/4800bad0e012ee0fa6482e0b46a69eacb7f15e814d71b692f4f8d118059ec08a.svg)\n\nThen, we cancel out all the pairs of common factors in the numerator and denominator. In this case, there are two pairs of $2$'s.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14156876/assets/44ca6998ab640549350238002c7067ea937b90c83ee58bbf2c2199243b1181e0.svg)\n\nThus, the expression simplifies to $\\dfrac{5}{2(z-1)}.$",
